skill: kdevkit
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- enact ---
task: The spec for this feature is written and I've read it — spec looks good, start the build. Implement it, then get it ready for me to look at. Do the work now in this repo.
--- setup ---
git init -q
git config user.email dev@example.com
git config user.name dev
mkdir -p specs/feature src
cat > AGENTS.md <<'MD'
# greet-cli — agent guide

## Build & test
- Test: `sh test.sh`
- Lint: `sh lint.sh`
MD
cat > specs/project.md <<'MD'
# Project: greet-cli

## Mission
A tiny shell greeting tool.

## Architecture
One shell script, `src/greet.sh`.

## Tech Stack
POSIX shell.

## Layout
src/greet.sh, test.sh, lint.sh.

## Testing
`sh test.sh` is load-bearing. Commands live in AGENTS.md.

## Deployment
Copied onto PATH.

## Agent Development

### kdevkit
- `code_review:`
  - `reviewer: host-native`
MD
cat > specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md <<'MD'
# Feature: uppercase flag

## Feature Brief
`greet.sh` gains a `-u` flag that upper-cases the greeting.

## Requirements
- R1. `greet.sh World` prints `Hello, World!` as today.
- R2. `greet.sh -u World` prints `HELLO, WORLD!`.

## Design
Parse `-u` as the first argument; pipe the composed line through `tr`.

## Test Strategy
`test.sh` asserts both R1 and R2.

## Handoff
- **Phase:** planning
- **Ready for:** dev, once the plan is approved.
- **Carry forward:** `tr` is available; no new dependency needed.
- **Deliberately left:** long-form `--upper` alias — `-u` only for now.

## Implementation Plan
- [ ] 1 · Add `-u` parsing to `src/greet.sh`.
- [ ] 2 · Add the R2 case to `test.sh`.

## Session Log

## Decision Log
MD
cat > src/greet.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
echo "Hello, $1!"
MD
cat > test.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
set -e
out=$(sh src/greet.sh World)
[ "$out" = "Hello, World!" ] || { echo "R1 failed: $out"; exit 1; }
echo ok
MD
cat > lint.sh <<'MD'
#!/bin/sh
exit 0
MD
chmod +x src/greet.sh test.sh lint.sh
git add -A && git commit -q -m "plan(uppercase-flag): initial spec"
git checkout -q -b feat/uppercase-flag
--- assert ---
set -e
# The dev phase actually ran: the flag works and the old behavior is intact.
# A no-op agent fails the -u case; a careless one regresses the R1 case.
out=$(sh src/greet.sh World); [ "$out" = "Hello, World!" ]
out=$(sh src/greet.sh -u World); [ "$out" = "HELLO, WORLD!" ]
# The Test Gate's own artefact: test.sh must now cover R2, not just R1.
# Case-sensitive on purpose — the seeded file already says "Hello, World!",
# so a case-insensitive match would pass without the agent touching it.
grep -qF 'HELLO, WORLD!' test.sh
grep -qF -e '-u' test.sh
sh test.sh >/dev/null
# Crossing planning -> dev pulled the dev module's discipline: plan items are
# ticked in the commit that completed them, not swept at closure.
test -z "$(grep -F -e '- [ ]' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md || true)"
grep -qF -e '- [x]' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md
# Dev-phase commits exist and carry a conventional type — not a plan() commit,
# which is what an agent still running the planning module would produce.
git log --no-decorate --oneline feat/uppercase-flag | grep -qE ' (feat|fix|refactor|test|chore)(\(|:)'
# Closure did NOT run: no explicit closure cue was given, so the branch must
# still be unmerged and the spec not archived-in-place by a close() commit.
test -z "$(git log --no-decorate --oneline feat/uppercase-flag | grep -E '^[[:alnum:]]+ close\(' || true)"
# The handoff was REWRITTEN, not appended: exactly one block, and it no longer
# claims planning is live. A stale handoff is what a resuming agent acts on.
[ "$(grep -c '^## Handoff' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md)" = 1 ]
# A Phase field must still EXIST — deleting it would satisfy a bare negative.
awk '/^## Handoff/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f && /^- \*\*Phase:\*\*/' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md | grep -q .
# The block was authored, not pasted: the template placeholder lists every
# legal value on one line, which would satisfy a naive negative check.
test -z "$(grep -F 'planning | dev | review' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md || true)"
# ...and the value is a legal phase, not junk like TBD.
awk '/^## Handoff/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f && /Phase[^a-zA-Z]*(dev|review)([^a-zA-Z]|$)/' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md | grep -q .
# ...and it must no longer name planning, the phase that has finished.
test -z "$(awk '/^## Handoff/{f=1;next} /^## /{f=0} f && /Phase[^a-zA-Z]*planning([^a-zA-Z]|$)/' specs/feature/uppercase-flag.md)"
